    "lawCode": "Amd §7-121, El L",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5448\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to ballots which are\ncounted by machine\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThe bill permits ballots for use in voting systems approved by the\nstate board of elections to be printed and arranged in a manner that\nwould permit them to be counted on such system.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends Election Law section 7-121 to provide that all\nballots printed for use on a voting system approved by the State Board\nof Elections may be printed and arranged in a manner which would\npermit them to be counted by such machine.\n\nSection 2: Provides for the Act to take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nElection Law section 7-121 currently provides that if ballots are cast\nat an election other than on the voting machines being used for it,\nthen a board of elections may provide for those ballots to be counted\non a machine of a type approved by the state board of elections, and\nthat all such ballots may be printed and arranged in a manner that\nwould enable them to be counted on such machine.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAlthough New York's full face ballot requirements remain intact, with\nthe implementation of optical scan voting systems in poll sites the\ninformation on ballots must be configured in a manner that will allow\nscanners to sufficiently and adequately discern votes cast by the\nvoters.  This bill deletes unnecessary language about the choice of\nvoting machines, which has already been made, and changes the focus of\nthe provision to making sure that the ballots to be used on new voting\nmachines will be able to be counted by them. Ballot information\nincludes instructions to voters, a variety of shapes for voting\npositions, candidates names, party endorsements, office titles, ballot\nproposals, party emblems, \"vote for:\" information, terms of office and\nother similar information.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n LOCAL.FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
